11. One more important consideration: Power integrity

Because this is an FPV flight controller, your PCB must handle electrical noise from switching regulators, motors, ESCs, and video transmission.

Consider the following:

1. Input protection

Appropriately rated fuse or other overcurrent protection
Reverse-polarity protection where required
Input capacitors selected according to the converter's requirements
Transient protection where appropriate

2. Power supply stability

Place decoupling capacitors close to IC power pins.
Follow each converter's recommended input/output capacitor values.
Verify voltage ripple and transient response under load.
Check startup behavior and power sequencing.

3. PCB layout

Keep switching-regulator high-current loops compact.
Use appropriate copper width and thickness for the expected current.
Provide a suitable ground-return path.
Keep sensitive sensor circuitry away from noisy switching nodes.
Follow the MCU and sensor manufacturers' layout recommendations.

4. Current capacity

For each power rail, calculate the expected load:

$$ I_{\text{rail}}=\sum_{k=1}^{n} I_k $$

where \(I_k\) is the current consumed by each component supplied by that rail.

Then select the converter with sufficient continuous-current capability, thermal margin, and transient capability.

Do not select a converter based only on its advertised maximum current; thermal conditions, input voltage, PCB copper, and component temperatures also affect the usable output current.

Final summary

Your FCNS block diagram shows how a battery-powered flight controller can distribute power to its MCU, sensors, navigation modules, camera, and other peripherals.

The four proposed power rails serve different purposes:

10 V: Camera supply, if compatible.
5 V: Receiver and selected peripheral supply.
3.3 V: MCU I/O and compatible sensors and peripherals.
1.2 V: MCU core supply, if required by the selected MCU.

The most important next step is to verify the exact MCU, sensors, camera, video transmitter, and receiver before finalizing the voltage rails. Then add the missing signal connections and specify the current requirement for each power rail.

This will turn your present power-distribution block diagram into a more complete, technically accurate FPV Flight Control and Navigation System architecture.
